# Generated reference data — NEVER committed.
#
# Two reasons, both non-negotiable:
#   1. It is other people's content. mccc_help.json is ~152 KB of Deaderpool's
#      verbatim MCCC tooltip strings; the *_schema.json files are setting names
#      and defaults extracted from MCCC and Kuttoe's mods.
#   2. It embeds local absolute paths (C:\Users\<account>\...), which would
#      publish the machine account name.
#
# All of it regenerates in seconds from a local install:
#     py sulskill-mccc/scripts/extract_schema.py
#     py sulskill-kuttoe/scripts/extract_kuttoe.py
# Generated files also drift out of date the moment a mod updates, so shipping
# the extractors rather than the extracts is the correct design regardless.
#
# Matched by filename, not by path. These were once anchored to the skill
# directories, and renaming those directories silently un-ignored all three -
# leaving other people's content staged to be published by the next `git add`.
# The filenames are distinctive; the paths were not worth the fragility.
mccc_help.json
mccc_schema.json
kuttoe_schema.json

# Backstop only. Generators write to gate.out_dir() (outside the checkout) and
# the report builders require an explicit --out, so nothing below should ever
# appear here. These patterns exist in case someone adds a tool that forgets.
# See sulskill/POLICY.md, "What belongs in this repository".
report.json
sulskill-doctor/reference/
# Console-command documents name every mod installed on one machine. The tools
# that build them ship; the output never does.
console-commands*.md
console-commands*.html
*_inventory.json
*_PLAN.txt

# Generated premade roster - EA game text (bios), regenerate with roster.py --rebuild
roster.json

# Local scratch and caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.bak
reports/

# Local review decisions about one machine's library. A judgement about what is
# installed here is not a fact about anyone else's install, so it never ships.
_shared/reviewed.local
_shared/scancache.local
